/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Repositories_MIDILAR MIDILAR
 * @ingroup RoModular_Repositories
 * @brief MIDI protocol, parsing, routing, timing and real-time devices.
 *
 * | Field | Value |
 * | ----- | ----- |
 * | Role | MIDI protocol data, parsing, routing, timing, transports and devices |
 * | Current release | [`v0.2.0`](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/MIDILAR/releases/tag/v0.2.0) |
 * | Status | Active; MIDI-CI deferred |
 * | Source | [ChecheRomo96/MIDILAR](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/MIDILAR) |
 * | Documentation | [MIDILAR on GitHub Pages](https://checheromo96.github.io/MIDILAR/) |
 * | Runtime dependencies | Foundation `1.4.0` or a newer 1.x release, MCC `0.5.2` or a newer 0.x release |
 * | Public CMake target | `MIDILAR::MIDILAR` |
 *
 * The legacy implementation had no consumers and was removed. MIDILAR was
 * rebuilt phase by phase from a MIDI-domain specification, on the same pinned
 * RoModularBuild `v0.4.0` as Foundation and MCC, and validated on an Arduino
 * Mega 2560. Release `0.2.0` contains:
 *
 * - Protocol: channels, groups and masks; note, controller and program
 *   numbers; values at MIDI 2.0 resolution; UMP packets; MIDI 1.0 byte-stream
 *   and USB MIDI 1.0 translation; MIDI Time Code; MCC pitch conversions.
 * - Devices: channel filter and reassignment, transposition, velocity curves,
 *   scale filter and chord generation on MCC, a router, MIDI clock, a
 *   Euclidean step sequencer and MTC.
 *
 * Hardware transports (UART, USB stacks, desktop MIDI APIs) will be separate
 * libraries built on MIDILAR's translations. MIDI-CI is deferred. Signal
 * processing belongs to @ref RoModular_Repositories_DspCore "DspCore".
 */
